.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt ETHERNET-AUTODETECT.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm ethernet-autodetect.sh
.Nd detect and configure an Ethernet uplink or wired user device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -hotplug
.Op Fl -iface Ar interface
.Op Fl -mode Cm gateway | wired-eud
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
examines carrier, DHCP and link traffic to select an Ethernet role.
An uplink with verified internet access stays routed and provides a mesh
gateway; a wired end-user device is bridged to
.Li br0 .
The access-point role follows the
.Li eud
setting in the node configuration.
Run as root; detection can change addresses, routes, bridge membership,
firewall rules and running network services.
.Pp
Without an interface override, the saved upstream interface is preferred,
then native
.Li end0 ,
then an available USB Ethernet interface.
An existing decision may be reused while the physical connection is unchanged.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -hotplug
Accept a hot-plug invocation; automatic detection is also the default.
.It Fl -iface Ar interface
Use the named interface.
.It Fl -mode Cm gateway | wired-eud
Request a role directly instead of automatic role detection.
Normal carrier and configuration checks still apply.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/mesh.conf
Node configuration, including the end-user-device mode.
.It Pa /var/run/upstream_iface
Selected upstream interface.
.It Pa /var/run/ethernet_detection_state
Recorded Ethernet role.
.It Pa /etc/systemd/network/
Interface configuration updated for the selected role.
.It Pa /var/log/ethernet-detect.log
Output from the latest run.
.It Pa /etc/eth-detect-debug
Its presence enables shell tracing and copies output to the caller.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 when handling completes, including when no role change is needed
or internet access is unavailable.
Exits nonzero for invalid arguments, lock timeout or a detected operating error.
A zero status does not prove internet connectivity.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Request a wired user-device connection on the native port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo ethernet-autodetect.sh --iface end0 --mode wired-eud
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr usb-wifi-uplink.sh 8 ,
.Xr verify-bridge.sh 8
